  <model metaid="meta_rapamycin_liver" id="rapamycin_liver" name="Model for hepatic rapamycin metabolism." substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <h1>Model for hepatic rapamycin metabolism</h1>
        <p>Rapamycin equilibrates fast between the blood and the liver and is
metabolized by CYP3A4 and CYP3A5 (<code>RAP2RX</code>), linear in the concentrations
of the therapeutic doses. The concentrations are those of whole blood:
about 95 % of the rapamycin of the blood is bound in the erythrocytes
(FKBP12), the intrinsic clearance is a clearance of whole blood. Rapamycin
has a low hepatic extraction (blood clearance about 3 l/hr against a
hepatic blood flow of about 90 l/hr).</p>
        <p>The metabolites are released into the blood (<code>RXEX</code>) and excreted into the
bile (<code>RXBEX</code>), from where they reach the lumen of the intestine and the
feces.</p>
        <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
