    <listOfParameters>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000009" id="RXBEX_k" name="rate of the biliary excretion of the rapamycin metabolites" value="0.15" units="per_min" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>The biliary clearance of the metabolites is about 5 times their renal
clearance (<code>KI__RXEX_k</code>): after an oral dose of 14C-rapamycin 91 % of
the radioactivity is recovered in the feces and 2.2 % in the urine
(Leung2006), and most of the fecal radioactivity is formed in the gut
wall or not absorbed.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000009" id="RAPIM_k" name="rate rapamycin import" value="100" units="per_min" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000009" id="RAP2RX_k" name="rate of rapamycin metabolism by CYP3A4" value="0.0261505045623823" units="per_min" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>Intrinsic clearance of CYP3A4 per volume of the liver, of
whole blood concentrations. The metabolism is linear: the Km of
the microsomes (8.07 µM, Sattler1992) is far above the
concentrations of the therapeutic doses.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
